/implement.jsonl",".trellis/tasks/archive/2026-08/08-01-pi-model-doctor-implementation/prd.md",".trellis/tasks/archive/2026-08/08-01-pi-model-doctor-implementation/task.json",".trellis/workflow.md",".trellis/workspace/index.md",".trellis/workspace/jiangge/index.md",".trellis/workspace/jiangge/journal-1.md","AGENTS.md","Pi_Model_Doctor_Implementation_Plan_v3.docx","README.md"],"architectural_claims":["The project-local .pi/extensions/model-doctor extension separates command parsing, domain orchestration, JSON persistence, cache access, capability normalization, and models.dev integration.","models.dev metadata is normalized into a local-first cache with conditional refresh and stale-cache fallback.","models.json mutations preserve unknown/user-owned fields and use ownership snapshots to prevent unsafe automatic overwrites.","Model capability resolution is metadata-driven with provider adapters and a generic fallback instead of a finite hard-coded model table.","Mutating operations are dry-run capable and write timestamped backups before atomic replacement."],"behavioral_changes":["Pi now registers /model-doctor add, list, check, fix, remove, and refresh commands from the project settings.","add discovers provider/model metadata, proposes or writes managed entries, and can use environment-variable API-key references.","check reports missing, stale, conflicting, and healthy managed fields without requiring network access for the local file.","fix repairs only safe managed fields and supports dry-run/fix-all behavior.","refresh updates the local models.dev cache while retaining a valid stale cache on network failure."],"api_changes":[{"kind":"added","surface":"cli","signature":"/model-doctor add|list|check|fix|remove|refresh with documented target, --dry-run, --api-key, and --force options","compatibility":"compatible"},{"kind":"added","surface":"config","signature":"PI_MODEL_DOCTOR_DIR, PI_MODEL_DOCTOR_MODELS_PATH, and PI_MODEL_DOCTOR_MODELS_DEV_URL environment configuration","compatibility":"compatible"}],"data_model_changes":[{"kind":"added","name":"_piModelDoctor metadata","location":"Pi models.json provider/model entries","compatibility":"compatible","migration_required":false,"migration_notes":"Existing entries remain valid; metadata is added only when an entry is managed by Model Doctor."},{"kind":"added","name":"models.dev local cache files","location":"~/.pi/model-doctor/{models,providers,policies}-cache.json","compatibility":"compatible","migration_required":false,"migration_notes":"Caches are created lazily and can be regenerated with refresh."}],"security_implications":["API keys are accepted as input but command output is secret-safe and prefers environment-variable references.","User-owned fields are not overwritten after a detected ownership conflict.","Backups and atomic writes reduce the risk of partial or irreversible models.json corruption."],"migration_notes":["No migration is required for existing models.json files; the extension reads JSONC and preserves existing fields.","Enablement is project-local through .pi/settings.json; other projects can copy the extension and registration entry."],"tags":["pi","pi-extension","model-doctor","models.json","models.dev","jsonc","atomic-write","offline-cache","capability-normalization","secret-safe"]},"turn_count":4,"sealed_at":"2026-08-01T04:58:39Z","evidence_complete":true,"worktree_status":"clean","sealed_at_branch":"master"}